# ── ML model weights & training corpora ───────────────────────────────────────
# These routinely exceed GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit and are reproducible
# artifacts, not source. Ignoring them keeps a monorepo commit from silently
# dragging hundreds of MB into history — which is easy to do here, because the
# repo root holds jarvis alongside ph_economic_ai and a pathspec-less
# `git commit` picks up whatever happens to be staged.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
pytorch_model*.bin
model*.bin
adapter_model.bin
optimizer.pt
scheduler.pt
rng_state.pth
scaler.pt

# Fine-tuning corpora and checkpoints
jarvis/Training/
jarvis/**/checkpoint-*/
jarvis/deepseek-*/
jarvis/jarvis-lora-adapter/

# ── Per-run social snapshots ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `engine/live_social.py` and `tools/refresh_social.py` write a dated file here on
# every live run, so without this the directory accumulates a new blob per run and
# they drift into commits unnoticed. Ignored BY PATTERN rather than by directory:
# the spec treats a frozen social snapshot as legitimate committed data, so a
# deliberately curated file under a different name can still be added with -f.
# A missing directory is handled: load_social_snapshot returns zero posts.
ph_economic_ai/assets/corpus/social/reddit_*.jsonl
ph_economic_ai/assets/corpus/social/trends_*.jsonl

# DOE source PDFs: ~250MB, rebuildable from artifacts/doe_price_cache.json
ph_economic_ai/benchmark/data/doe_cache/
.superpowers/

# Machine-local run records from the refresh tools (see tools/run_log.py).
logs/
